---
layout: base.njk
bodyClass: "home-template is-head-left-logo has-cover"
---


<!-- Casper Hero Header -->
<div class="site-header-content outer">
    {% if site.coverImage %}
    <img class="site-header-cover"
        src="{{ site.coverImage }}"
        alt="{{ site.title }}"
        fetchpriority="high"
        loading="eager"
    />
    {% endif %}

    <div class="site-header-inner inner">
        {% if site.status %}
        <div class="status-pill">{{ site.status }}</div>
        {% endif %}
        <h1 class="site-title">{{ site.title }}</h1>
        {% if site.description %}
        <p class="site-description">{{ site.description }}</p>
        {% endif %}
        {% set cfpOpen = site.cfp.status == "open" and site.cfp.url %}
        {% set ticketsOpen = site.tickets.status == "open" and site.tickets.url %}
        {% if cfpOpen or ticketsOpen %}
        <div class="hero-actions">
            {% if ticketsOpen %}
            <a class="hero-button" href="{{ site.tickets.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ site.tickets.buttonText }}</a>
            {% endif %}
            {% if cfpOpen %}
            <a class="hero-button{% if ticketsOpen %} is-secondary{% endif %}" href="{{ site.cfp.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ site.cfp.buttonText }}</a>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
        {% if cfpOpen and site.cfp.deadline %}
        <p class="hero-note">{{ site.cfp.label }} open until {{ site.cfp.deadline }}</p>
        {% endif %}
        {% elif site.cfp.status == "closed" %}
        <p class="hero-note">{{ site.cfp.label }} is closed. Thank you to everyone who submitted.</p>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
</div>

<main id="site-main" class="site-main">

    <!-- Newsletter / Subscribe Call to Action -->
    <section id="subscribe" class="footer-cta outer subscribe-section">
        <div class="inner">
            <h2 class="footer-cta-title">{{ site.newsletter.title }}</h2>
            <p style="max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto 28px; font-size: 1.7rem; color: var(--color-secondary-text);">
                {{ site.newsletter.description }}
            </p>

            <form id="subscribe-form" class="footer-cta-form" action="{{ site.newsletter.action }}" method="POST">
                <input
                    type="email"
                    name="{{ site.newsletter.emailFieldName }}"
                    placeholder="Enter your email address"
                    aria-label="Email address"
                    required
                />
                <button type="submit">{{ site.newsletter.buttonText }}</button>
            </form>
            <div id="subscribe-feedback" class="subscribe-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
            {% if site.newsletter.privacyNote %}
            <p class="subscribe-privacy">
                {{ site.newsletter.privacyNote }} <a href="/datenschutz/#newsletter">Privacy details</a>
            </p>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- About Section -->
    <section id="about" class="outer about-section">
        <div class="inner about-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">What is DevFest?</h2>
            <p class="about-text">
                DevFests are community-led developer events hosted by Google Developer Groups worldwide.
                DevFest Berlin brings together engineers, designers, and tech leaders for talks, workshops,
                and networking across Android, Web, Cloud, AI, and more.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Date & Venue Section -->
    <section id="venue" class="outer venue-section">
        <div class="inner">
            <div class="venue-card">
                <div class="venue-item">
                    <span class="venue-badge">Confirmed Date</span>
                    <h3 class="venue-title">Saturday, November 14, 2026</h3>
                    <p class="venue-subtitle">Full-day conference with keynote talks, sessions & workshops</p>
                </div>
                <div class="venue-divider"></div>
                <div class="venue-item">
                    <span class="venue-badge">Host Venue</span>
                    <h3 class="venue-title">SRH Berlin</h3>
                    <p class="venue-subtitle">SRH Berlin University of Applied Sciences &bull; Ernst-Reuter-Platz &bull; Berlin, Germany</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Conference Tracks Section -->
    <section id="tracks" class="outer tracks-section">
        <div class="inner">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2 class="section-title">2026 Conference Tracks</h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">
                    Whether you are an experienced software engineer or a creative product builder, DevFest Berlin 2026 has dedicated learning paths for you.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="tracks-grid">
                <div class="track-card">
                    <div>
                        <span class="track-pill">Core Track</span>
                        <h3>Tech Talks & Keynotes</h3>
                        <p>Deep-dive architecture sessions and best practices delivered by international industry leaders and Google Developer Experts.</p>
                        <ul class="track-highlights">
                            <li>Modern Android & Jetpack Compose</li>
                            <li>Cloud Native, Go & Kubernetes</li>
                            <li>Flutter & Multiplatform Development</li>
                            <li>Production Machine Learning & Web Performance</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="track-card">
                    <div>
                        <span class="track-pill">Builder Track</span>
                        <h3>App Development for Everyone</h3>
                        <p>Empowering developers, designers, product managers, and founders to rapidly build and ship prototypes using modern AI tooling.</p>
                        <ul class="track-highlights">
                            <li>Prototyping with Google AI Studio & Gemini</li>
                            <li>Building AI apps with Google Ecosystem & Maps</li>
                            <li>Visual app generation & low-code workflows</li>
                            <li>From idea to deployed Android & Web applications</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="track-card">
                    <div>
                        <span class="track-pill">Developer Track</span>
                        <h3>Gemini Enterprise Agent Ready</h3>
                        <p>Advanced hands-on labs and architectural sessions exploring agentic workflows, multimodal retrieval, and scalable AI infrastructure.</p>
                        <ul class="track-highlights">
                            <li>Agent Development Kit (ADK) & Agent Platform</li>
                            <li>Multimodal RAG with Gemini 1.5 & Gemini 2.0</li>
                            <li>Deploying and governing production-ready agents</li>
                            <li>High-performance multi-agent architectures</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Hackathon Section -->
    <section id="hackathon" class="outer hackathon-section">
        <div class="inner">
            <div class="feature-card">
                <div class="feature-header">
                    <div class="feature-title-group">
                        <span class="feature-badge">All-Day Sprint</span>
                        <h3>DevFest Berlin 2026 Hackathon</h3>
                    </div>
                    <div class="action-chip">
                        Theme: Practical Solutions to Real-World Problems
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p style="font-size: 1.6rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-secondary-text); margin: 0 0 20px;">
                    Join fellow builders, designers, and students in a dedicated hackathon space on the SRH Berlin campus. Collaborate in teams to conceptualize, build, and pitch functioning software addressing tangible everyday challenges.
                </p>

                <div class="feature-grid">
                    <div class="feature-item">
                        <h4>Tooling & Credits</h4>
                        <p>Generous platform credits and development tooling provided by partner platforms including Lovable and Beast44.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="feature-item">
                        <h4>Student Friendly</h4>
                        <p>Special free ticket allocations and dedicated student mentorship in collaboration with GDG on Campus SRH Berlin.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="feature-item">
                        <h4>Prizes & Demos</h4>
                        <p>Pitch your live prototypes on stage to an expert jury. Win physical gear, credits, and community recognition.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="feature-footer-actions">
                    <span class="action-chip">&bull; Mentors on-site</span>
                    <span class="action-chip">&bull; High-speed Wi-Fi & power</span>
                    <span class="action-chip">&bull; Catering included</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Vibe Lounge Section -->
    <section id="vibe-lounge" class="outer vibe-lounge-section">
        <div class="inner">
            <div class="feature-card">
                <div class="feature-header">
                    <div class="feature-title-group">
                        <span class="feature-badge vibe-badge">Guided Hands-On</span>
                        <h3>Official DevFest Vibe Lounge</h3>
                    </div>
                    <div class="action-chip">
                        45-Minute Sprints &bull; Powered by Gemini
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p style="font-size: 1.6rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-secondary-text); margin: 0 0 20px;">
                    Step into our casual, high-energy vibecoding space designed for quick inspiration and live creation. Drop in for an assigned 45-minute sprint, tackle a creative challenge with Google AI Studio and Gemini, and walk away with a working app and the official DevFest badge.
                </p>

                <div class="feature-grid">
                    <div class="feature-item">
                        <h4>Backyard Barista</h4>
                        <p>Design and deploy a bespoke coffee recommendation or order-taking assistant powered by multimodal Gemini prompts.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="feature-item">
                        <h4>Multiplayer Games</h4>
                        <p>Generate interactive browser-based games or quiz battles in minutes using AI assistance and Web APIs.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="feature-item">
                        <h4>Google Maps & AI</h4>
                        <p>Blend geolocation intelligence with generative insights to build local discovery and city guides.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="feature-footer-actions">
                    <a class="action-chip" href="https://goo.gle/devfest26-vibe-lounge" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 700;">
                        Claim Vibe Lounge Badge: goo.gle/devfest26-vibe-lounge &rarr;
                    </a>
                    <span class="action-chip">&bull; Guided by on-site mentors</span>
                    <span class="action-chip">&bull; No prior coding required</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Organizers Section -->
    <section id="organizers" class="outer organizers-section">
        <div class="inner">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2 class="section-title">Community Organizers</h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">
                    DevFest Berlin is collaboratively organized by local tech communities.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="organizers-grid">
                {% for org in site.organizers %}
                <div class="organizer-card">
                    <div>
                        <h3>{{ org.name }}</h3>
                        <p>{{ org.description }}</p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <a class="card-link" href="{{ org.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                            Join Community &rarr;
                        </a>
                    </div>
                </div>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Sponsors Section -->
    <section id="sponsors" class="outer sponsors-section">
        <div class="inner">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2 class="section-title">{{ site.sponsorship.title }}</h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">{{ site.sponsorship.pitch }}</p>
            </div>
            {% if site.sponsors.length %}
            {% include "partials/sponsor-wall.njk" %}
            {% endif %}
            <p class="sponsors-action">
                <a class="sponsor-button" href="/sponsors/">Become a sponsor</a>
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ Section -->
    <section id="faq" class="outer faq-section">
        <div class="inner">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">
                    Got questions? Here is everything you need to know about DevFest Berlin 2026.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-accordion">
                <details class="faq-item">
                    <summary>How do I get to SRH Berlin University of Applied Sciences?</summary>
                    <div class="faq-answer">
                        <p>SRH Berlin is located right at <strong>Ernst-Reuter-Platz</strong> in Charlottenburg, Berlin. The venue is easily accessible via public transport:</p>
                        <p>&bull; <strong>U-Bahn:</strong> U2 (Station Ernst-Reuter-Platz, just 1 minute walk).<br>&bull; <strong>S-Bahn:</strong> S3, S5, S7, S9 (Tiergarten or Zoologischer Garten, 10–12 minutes walk).<br>&bull; <strong>Bus:</strong> M45, 245, 101 directly stopping at Ernst-Reuter-Platz.</p>
                    </div>
                </details>

                <details class="faq-item">
                    <summary>Are there free or discounted tickets for students?</summary>
                    <div class="faq-answer">
                        <p>Yes! DevFest Berlin believes in making tech education accessible. In partnership with <strong>GDG on Campus SRH Berlin</strong>, we offer dedicated free and heavily subsidized student tickets. You will simply need to verify your enrollment with a valid student email address or student ID during registration.</p>
                    </div>
                </details>

                <details class="faq-item">
                    <summary>When does the Call for Speakers (CFP) close?</summary>
                    <div class="faq-answer">
                        <p>The Call for Speakers is open through <strong>October 15, 2026</strong> on Sessionize. We welcome talk proposals across Mobile, Web, Cloud, AI, and developer tooling. Speaker selections will be announced in late October.</p>
                    </div>
                </details>

                <details class="faq-item">
                    <summary>What is the Vibe Lounge and do I need prior coding experience?</summary>
                    <div class="faq-answer">
                        <p>The Vibe Lounge is an interactive 45-minute building sprint where attendees get hands-on with Google Gemini and Google AI Studio. No prior coding experience is required! On-site mentors guide you through prompt engineering, app generation, and deploying real solutions. Completing a challenge earns you an official Google DevFest Vibe Lounge badge.</p>
                    </div>
                </details>

                <details class="faq-item">
                    <summary>Who can participate in the DevFest Hackathon?</summary>
                    <div class="faq-answer">
                        <p>The Hackathon is open to all conference attendees, including students, developers, and designers. You can form teams on the day or sign up with friends. Hardware, tooling credits, and mentorship will be provided on-site.</p>
                    </div>
                </details>

                <details class="faq-item">
                    <summary>When will ticket sales open and will there be Google Cloud credits?</summary>
                    <div class="faq-answer">
                        <p>Tickets will open shortly with Early Bird discounts. Attendees will also receive access to Google Cloud credits for hands-on learning and workshop participation.</p>
                    </div>
                </details>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

</main>
